  "instance_name": "bird_nickname_culture",
  "label": "bird nickname culture",
  "description": "A cultural phenomenon where people assign informal, often humorous or affectionate nicknames to birds or other animals based on their appearance, behavior, or habitat. This is common in social media, memes, and casual conversation, and often serves to humanize or anthropomorphize animals. The term 'beach chickens' fits into this category as a playful rebranding.",
